WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.340
If TMC1 lines the pore, why does the current also depend on other proteins?

2
00:00:09.483 --> 00:00:14.563
No native mammalian structure was available, so Jeong, Clark and colleagues turned

3
00:00:14.563 --> 00:00:15.563
to a worm.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:23.137
They purified the native TMC-1 complex from C. elegans, and solved it by cryo-EM.

5
00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:29.730
The main assembly held two copies each of TMC-1, CALM-1, and TMIE.

6
00:00:30.683 --> 00:00:35.143
CALM-1 is the worm relative of the mammalian protein CIB2.

7
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:40.983
The human complex in that paper was a model built on the worm structure, not a

8
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:41.983
measurement.

9
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.873
Read the mouse partners through the three factors.

10
00:00:45.793 --> 00:00:52.273
Without CIB2, cochlear stereocilia showed no detectable TMC1 or TMC2.

11
00:00:52.833 --> 00:00:54.613
So the channel count at the site falls.

12
00:00:55.617 --> 00:01:01.377
Without TMIE, tagged TMC1 could not be detected in the stereocilia either.

13
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:08.630
Predict. Overexpressed TMC1 still reaches the stereocilia there, yet gives no

14
00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:10.890
current. What does that tell you?

15
00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:20.703
TMIE is needed for more than getting TMC1 there.

16
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:23.943
It may help build, couple or gate a working channel.

17
00:01:24.967 --> 00:01:29.647
Deafness-linked TMIE mutations also lowered the unitary current.

18
00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:35.107
In cells where TMC2 carried the current, they changed calcium permeability.

19
00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.870
So TMIE shapes the pore's properties, without being shown to be the pore.

20
00:01:42.853 --> 00:01:46.553
LHFPL5 binds the tip-link protein PCDH15.

21
00:01:47.493 --> 00:01:51.533
Without it, Xiong and colleagues saw smaller single-channel events in 2012.

22
00:01:52.633 --> 00:01:58.653
Later recordings with TMC1-only channels found no change, so its molecular effect is

23
00:01:58.653 --> 00:01:59.653
still open.

24
00:02:00.217 --> 00:02:04.017
The current you measure belongs to the complex, not to one protein.

25
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:08.010
Even a complete ladder leaves one question open.

26
00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:10.890
How does force from the tip link reach the pore?

27
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.663
Of each experiment, ask which factor it tested.

28
00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:18.083
The case for the pore rests on several rungs together.
